<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.law.indexes ~ the house's law, pinned law first, from the worn face's daemon wiki

The index derives from canon by filter and no list stands in code. The pin set (`$:/config/lares/law/pins`, a TiddlyWiki filter the wiki's own engine runs) heads it in its own order, the boot seed then the Mu family; then every root meme under a bag's `api/` tree the pins leave out follows, by title, each with its one line (the meme's description, else its role). Only canon prints: a row stands where a canon layer answers its record, so nothing a face writes reads as law.

Read it before you act, the way you read your working memory. A law row comes from canon's settled ground; turn it through the five tools.

One page holds at most 32 rows, and `next` names the cursor of the page behind (hand it back as `after`; `all` follows every cursor to the end). Both doors answer one shape: {filter, pinsTitle, pins, rows: [{title, description, pinned}], total, next}. A terminal prints it plainly (the pinned titles marked 📌, then the law they leave out) and `json=true` carries the body the seat returns.

Read one law whole through the read door: `lares get title=<title> aperture=arc` on a terminal, `get(title=<title>, aperture="arc")` on the seat. Order the pins with `engine.law.pins` and `engine.law.unpins`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ first-page · every-row · a-page-behind

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`first-page` params=`~ the first page: pins, then law by title`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`every-row` params=`all/true ~ every row, page after page (json=true answers {filter, pinsTitle, pins, rows, total, next})`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-page-behind` params=`limit/10 after/<cursor> ~ ten rows behind the cursor a prior answer named in next`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ limit · after · all · face

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`limit` params=`takes/count ~ rows per page; the door's ceiling of 32 holds`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`after` params=`takes/cursor ~ the page behind a cursor a prior answer named in next`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`all` params=`kind/switch ~ follow every cursor to the end and answer every row`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a read: the index runs the tiddler door's wiki-filter in the worn face's daemon wiki and writes nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ index

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`index` params=`exit/0 fields/[[filter pinsTitle pins rows total next]] ~ the pinned titles, then the law they leave out; each row reads {title, description, pinned}; next names the cursor of the page behind, null at the end`>>
```

